          "source_lines": "SameQCountEntrance27-122; J/P5OriginalU5FrozenSource26-102; J/h34 frozen source",
          "finding": "The receiver is exactly ell.Coprime N on the original additive-prime label and remains fixed through descendants. Selected-prime primality and J cutoff<=p derive ChenPrimeRough cutoff p; this discharges the essential mask-removal premise. The frozen count then equals the actual chenSiftedQuotientPrimeSource cardinality. Unit quotients, centre deletion, strict U3/U4 upper bands and their multiplicity-two overlap are preserved."
        },
        {
          "area": "Unchanged row Q and arithmetic state",
          "source_lines": "SameQCountEntrance43-184; I/P2AllW2ImmutableCountRecursion",
          "finding": "For t=log(p)/log(N), Q=N^(t+L) gives Q/p=N^L. Actual branches give residual in[1/12,1/2], Q<=N^(153/256)<=N and root query at least2. The joint state keeps this Q and original receiver while all ordinary/W1/W2 alternatives read one immutable old state. The exported Encloses invariant is derived by induction from genuine Rosser polynomials; no old-state invariant or count bound is a K premise. Raw switched, complement, tail, collision and bad-prime costs remain in the imported arithmetic state."
        },
        {
          "area": "Complete signed error identity",
          "source_lines": "PrimeCorrectionPayment29-65; J/P5OriginalU5FrozenSource147-196",
          "finding": "rowError equals rowSharpError minus the sum of rho(q)*(primeDivisorCount(N,p*q)/phi(p*q)+centrePrimeAPCount(N,N,p*q)). Both corrections use the complete modulus p*q, so the selected prime p is included in the modulus-prime loss. The same signed rho is retained in the primitive sharp discrepancy and pi(N)-li(N) shift. No correction is deleted or made positive before taking an absolute bound."
        },
        {
          "area": "Actual deterministic bound",
          "source_lines": "PrimeCorrectionPayment67-270",
          "finding": "Nonzero Rosser support gives1<=q<=floor(Q/p), |rho(q)|<=1 and0<p*q<=Q<=N. Hence at most N^(1/2) active divisors occur per row. Distinct-prime product bounds and phi(p*q)>=1 give the two nonnegative correction atoms together at most2 log(N)/log(2). Each original band has at most N^(1/3) labels. Summing both complete bands gives exactly (4/log(2))*N^(5/6)*log(N), with their overlap counted twice. The support and error bounds are derived, not assumed, and use no enhanced distribution theorem."
        },
        {
          "area": "Uniformity and normalization",
          "source_lines": "SameQCountEntrance140-184; PrimeCorrectionPayment273-297; PowerErrorBudget49-88",
          "finding": "The ordinary seed threshold depends on eta and the fixed residual power1/12, before N, U, p, r, bank and rounds. The deterministic correction threshold precedes tau in[0,1/12] and either Bool sign. Proven power-log decay and the actual singular-series lower bound give both arbitrary logarithmic accuracy and epsilon*singularNormalization(N), without a PNT, normalization, or error-smallness premise."
        },
        {
